# Playwright e2e

Live `favlo web` (`127.0.0.1:8012`) and `favlo serve` (`8129`). Do not stub the model. Prefer `step` from `e2e/progress.ts`. Call `onScreen` before the completing click. Use `exact: true` on `Send`, `Home`, and workspace names. Do not pipe runs through `tail`.

## Timeouts (15 seconds)

A hung step must fail within **15 seconds**. Do not pass `timeout: 60_000` / `180_000` / `360_000` on `expect`, `poll`, `waitForEvent`, or `test.setTimeout` for a single wait. `playwright.config.ts` sets `expect.timeout`, `actionTimeout`, and `navigationTimeout` to 15s. Override only downward. A slow model load or a dead serve is a failed step to investigate, not a longer wait.

## Teardown

Every script that creates an agent or workspace deletes it in `finally`, even when the test fails.

- Agents: `deleteAgentsNamed` from `e2e/cleanup.ts` (never delete Favlo).
- Workspaces: `deleteWorkspacesNamed` from `e2e/cleanup.ts`.
- Temp folders: `fs.rmSync(..., { recursive: true, force: true })`.
- Do not leave Align/Place/Session/Stills/Bind/Frame/Captions-style names on disk or in the API after the run.

## User chat

Type what a person would type. Do not put tool names, schemas, or `workspace_place` / `gallery_find_*` recipes in the message box. A stalled agent gets one natural-language nudge, then fail.

## Channels and Home

Clicking an already-expanded channel **collapses** it. Wait for `Home` (or `aria-expanded="true"`) before clicking Favlo. Scope Home under `getByLabel('Channels')`. When a gallery is open, click `Back to channel` first. On a narrow viewport, open the Channels drawer before a workspace row.

## AG-UI and Stop

After Send for ordinary chat, wait until `POST /ag-ui` returns OK before Stop so the user message is persisted. Prefer letting a reply finish before `/session archive`; a client abort can leave a running run that blocks archive. `/session clear` and `/session archive` do not need the AG-UI wait helper used for chat text.

## Gallery chat UI

Workspace transcript uses `transcriptFrame(space[4])` like home. Assert the latest turn sits on the composer when the script covers chat layout.

## WCAG AA

Use `assertWcagAa` from `e2e/a11y.ts` (axe `wcag2a` / `wcag2aa` / `wcag21*` / `wcag22aa`). Cover light and dark on screens that own text-heavy chrome (folder bind at minimum). Text and control colors come from `palette` / `textStyle`.

## Suite runs

Fail fast (`set -eo pipefail`). One Chromium project. Re-check serve `200` between specs when chaining. Gallery scripts skip coding workspaces.
